aviors, morbidity, and cause-specific mortality in the United States: an analysis of two national data bases</article-title><source>Hum Biol</source><year>2002</year><volume>74</volume><fpage>83</fpage><lpage>109</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11931581</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lauderdale</surname><given-names>DS</given-names></name><name><surname>Rathouz</surname><given-names>PJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Body mass index in a US national sample of Asian Americans: effects of nativity, years since immigration and socioeconomic status</article-title><source>Int J Obes Relat Metab Disord</source><year>2000</year><volume>24</volume><fpage>1188</fpage><lpage>1194</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11033989</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bennett</surname><given-names>GG</given-names></name><name><surname>Wolin</surname><given-names>KY</given-names></name><name><surname>Askew</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Fletcher</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Emmons</surname><given-names>KM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Immigration and obesity among lower income blacks</article-title><source>Obesity (Silver Spring, Md</source><year>2007</year><volume>15</volume><fpage>1391</fpage><lpage>1394</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17557975</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Khan</surname><given-names>LK</given-names></name><name><surname>Sobal</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Martorell</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Acculturation, socioeconomic status, and obesity in Mexican Americans, Cuban Americans, and Puerto Ricans</article-title>